# Archives -- never commit these. A 57.9 MB DUNCS.7z was committed in 5824204 and deleted
# again later, but git keeps every version ever committed, so .git still carries it and is
# 275 MB as a result. Removing the file a second time reclaims nothing; only rewriting those
# commits would, and that was declined. These rules stop it happening again.
*.7z
*.zip
*.rar
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# Generated GUI artifacts. Both are BUILT from data/simulations/results by
# deck/export_gui_data.py and deck/gui/build_gui.py, and change on every benchmark run --
# about 1.8 MB of churn per rebuild if tracked. The editable source doa_verify.html stays
# tracked; these two do not. Rebuild them with deck/gui/rebuild_gui.cmd.
deck/gui/doa_verify_data.json
deck/gui/doa_verify_inline.html

# Model checkpoints and trace archives, wherever they land
*.pt
*.npz
